      "writtenOn": "2014-07-31T20:40:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should not be a dummy value but rather a default value, that can be over written as you still need to be able to put any federated user into any domain via the mapping rules. Otherwise how does a federated user become a member of any domain, including the default domain?",
      "revId": "35335af68145d5807dc5daea8399f91b69958e50",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "baada198_8e4b4f5e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-07-31T20:56:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The domain of the *user* should not be touched by the mapping rules. Why does a federated user need to be \"a member of a domain\"? The mapping rules will map the user to a group (and a scope) and that group conveys the RBAC support to act on projects, domains, etc.\n\nIs there a reason a user *needs* to be considered owned by a domain? Being attached to a domain does not convey roles, authorization, etc. I don\u0027t see the value in having the user data structure reference the domain unless that user is actually managed by the domain directly (not the case with federation).",
      "parentUuid": "baada198_2bc5d53c",
      "revId": "35335af68145d5807dc5daea8399f91b69958e50",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "baada198_4e005703",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 6534
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-07-31T21:34:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So if I have understood correctly this fix is nothing to do with authz, and  will not effect the domains and projects a user can be a member of as a result of his roles and groups (and attribute mappings).This fix is purely cosmetic since some existing code expects all users to be managed by some domain administrator or other and expects the user domain field to be present. So you are reserving the keyword Federated to signify the domain of federated users.\n\nI therefore suggest you change \"dummy value of\" into \"reserved value of\"",
      "parentUuid": "baada198_8e4b4f5e",
      "revId": "35335af68145d5807dc5daea8399f91b69958e50",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
